OpenVerify NFC module (openverify-nfc)

This module is shipped separately from the OpenVerify core Android SDK
(openverify-sdk). The core SDK is licensed under the Apache License 2.0
and does not depend on this module.

This module's own code is licensed under LGPL-3.0 (LGPL-3.0-or-later).

The module holds OpenVerify's reader of the chip in electronic passports
and identity cards. It declares the android.permission.NFC permission and
the android.hardware.nfc feature (not required). It depends on the
libraries below by Maven coordinates, never shaded or copied: its AAR
holds none of their code, and an app that adds the module receives them
through the module's POM.


