The two SCUBA files

OpenVerify's licence rule refuses GPL code. A narrow, recorded exception
was granted on 2026-11-08 under the owner's delegation (Phase 10 owner
item P1, docs/plans/phase-10.plan.md, "Orchestrator decisions before
Workflow 10A"): CommandAPDU.java and ResponseAPDU.java, unmodified, taken
from Maven Central inside scuba-smartcards, only in this optional
artifact. The Classpath exception lets independent modules link these
files on their own terms.

Licence of the two files: GPL-2.0-only WITH Classpath-exception-2.0

Source location of the two files:
  https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/net/sf/scuba/scuba-smartcards/0.0.21/
  scuba-smartcards-0.0.21-sources.jar
  (net/sf/scuba/smartcards/CommandAPDU.java and ResponseAPDU.java)

Source of the other libraries: the sources jars beside each artifact on
Maven Central, for the versions above.


What a distributor takes on (not legal advice)

Because of these dependencies, this module is kept out of the core SDK.
Distributors of an app that includes this module must meet the LGPL terms
for JMRTD, SCUBA and cert-cvc, including letting users replace them with
modified versions and not forbidding the reverse engineering needed to
debug such a replacement, and the GPL-2.0 with Classpath exception terms
for the two SCUBA files. The module's consumer rules keep those libraries
whole and under their own names in a minified app, so that they stay
replaceable. An app that does not include this module distributes none of
this code. The module's README says more.
